  "analysis": "The anterior pituitary gland, also known as the adenohypophysis, is regulated hormonally by releasing hormones from the hypothalamus. It is not part of the hypothalamus, does not release ADH and oxytocin (which are released by the posterior pituitary or neurohypophysis), and is not formed by neurons but by endocrine cells. The anterior pituitary communicates with the hypothalamus through the hypophyseal portal system, not directly with the neurohypophysis. Therefore, the most accurate statement is that the anterior pituitary is regulated hormonally.",
